.Im MicroEmacs command|file
.ds C0 "(\fB\*(cX\*ch\fR)\ \&
.so me.tni
.TH find-hfile 3
.XI find-hfile - "\*(C0Load a file using selected handler"
.XI find-cfile - "Load an encrypted file"
.SH NAME
.Me "|find-hfile"
find-hfile \- Load a file using selected handler
.br
.Me "|find-cfile"
find-cfile \- Load an encrypted file
.Me $a
.SH SYNOPSIS
.na
.I n
.B find-hfile
"\fIh\fR" "\fIfile-name\fR" \*(C0
.br
.I n
.B find-cfile
"\fIfile-name\fR"
.ad
.SH DESCRIPTION
\fBfind-hfile\fR first prompts the user for the read handler \fIh\fR required to load the file into \*(mS, where
\fIh\fR can be:
.IP \fBC\fR
As with \fBc\fR below except that the user is prompted for a second handler which is combined with crypt. Supported
secondary handlers are \fBb\fR, \fBr\fR and \fBt\fR. When used this handler must be given first.
.IP \fBb\fR
Standard binary file handler, see 
.Ht binary 2m
mode for more information.
.IP \fBc\fR
Encrypted file handler, see 
.Ht crypt 2m
mode for more information.
.IP \fBr\fR
Reduced binary file handler, see 
.Ht rbin 2m
mode for more information.
.IP \fBt\fR
Normal text file, equivalent to standard use of
.Ht find-file 2 .
The file's encoding is detected, see
.Ht $buffer-encoding 5
to read it with a different one.
.IP \fBz\fR
Zip file handler, see 
.Ht find-zfile 3
for more information. This handler cannot currently be combined with \fBC\fR.
.PP
The macro then calls the appropriate underlying file handler command with the required numerical argument to load \fIfile-name\fR
correctly.
.PP
\fBfind-cfile\fR provides a simple interface to loading files in
.Ht crypt 2m
mode. The numeric argument has the same effect as with the
.Ht find-file 2
command except the \fBcrypt\fP mode is always enabled. See documentation on the mode and \fBfind-file\fR command for
more information.
.SH NOTES
\fBfind-hfile\fR and \fBfind-cfile\fR are macros defined in file \fCtools.emf\fR.
.PP
Buffers containing directory listings generated by \fBfind-file\fR and zip content listings created by
\fBfind-zfile\fR provide a similar interface to \fBfind-hfile\fR bound to the letter \fBh\fR. 
.PP
The command
.Ht find-file 2
is bound to key "\fC\*(cX9\fR" with a numeric argument of 3, this is equivalent to executing \fBfind-bfile\fR with no
argument.
.SH "SEE ALSO"
.na
